#
# flag.obj - Flag sheet, quad faces, two sided
#
# Geometry:   a flat sheet on the xy plane at z = 0, 1.6 by 1.0, which is the
#             16:10 of SFS 1982:269, centred on the origin.
# Components: 693 vertices, 693 UV coordinates, 1386 vertex normals, and 1280 quad
#             faces: 32 by 20 quads, each present twice, once in each winding.
#             A sheet is seen from both sides and the renderer culls back faces,
#             so the reverse copy is what keeps a fold from opening a hole. The
#             pair for a quad is adjacent, front first, in row major order, which
#             is what lets a demo find the cell a face lies in.
#
#             The normals come in two sets, the second the negation of the first,
#             and a face takes the set for the side it is. A vertex on a two
#             sided sheet has opposite normals front and back, and one shared set
#             would cancel to nothing the moment they were averaged together.
#
#             The mesh is flat and carries no wave. A demo writes z per vertex
#             and takes the normals again, so what is stored here is the sheet's
#             own, square on.
# Used by:    flatshadedflag, gouraudshadedflag.
#
o flag
